  "limits": [
    "PHP substitutes persistent constants such as NAN and PHP_INT_MAX while compiling; Phego leaves them for execution, so [NAN . ''] lacks its compile warning. Excluded from the fixture and listed in docs/decisions/compatibility-php8512.md.",
    "SPL classes such as ArrayObject have no inheritance metadata before W-29; static covariance cases use equivalent user classes.",
    "Constant expressions fold a class operand before PHP checks it, so const X = (A::class)::C; compiles in PHP but not in Phego; ('static')::C lacks PHP's invalid class name error."
  ],
  "review_status": "All nine PR #129 review comments on 3da26d5 were reproduced with the pinned images and fixed with failing-first regression cases."
